articles.body:
The **Audit Modules** menu group gives a focused view of engagements for three domains: **System/IT Audit**, **Financial Audit** and **Compliance Audit**. They are the *same engagements* as Audit Lifecycle → Engagements, filtered to one domain, with a header that states the control frameworks that apply.

![System/IT Audit workspace](/help/domain-it.jpg)

On a domain page you will see:

- a description and the control frameworks in scope (for IT: ISO 27001, ISO 22301, SOX ITGC, baselines, CAB change, DR & capacity);
- a **System audit toolkit** shortcut (IT domain) to the seven system-audit activities;
- counters – **Engagements**, **In progress**, **Overdue**;
- the filtered engagement list (search, status, priority);
- a **Start System/IT audit** button that opens the Start-audit wizard with the domain pre-selected.
